## What I changed

`scripts/check_assertion_weakening.py` (only file with logic):

Step 1 — the predicate. is_dedicated_test_file was path.startswith("tests/") or path.endswith("_tests.rs"). I confirmed both defects by re-running the control pair before touching anything: identical hunk body, path=tests/x.rs printed the skipped line, path=tokio/tests/x.rs printed nothing. Now it's "tests" in path.split("/")[:-1] or path.endswith("_tests.rs") — a path segment, so a cargo workspace's <crate>/tests/*.rs is recognised and the last component (src/tests.rs, bare tests.rs) is not.

Step 2 — the names. SKIPPED_UNKNOWN_VOCABULARY was documented as feeding --assert-macro/--test-macro but printed no names. Now two NAME-extracting twins (MACRO_NAME_RE, ATTR_NAME_RE — the old MACRO_CALL_RE is untouched) feed a sorted, de-duplicated, cap-stated-in-band line directly under the count. The cap is on names, never bytes, so the cut always falls between whole names. Names the vocabulary already matches are filtered out. Nothing prints when there's nothing to name.

One rule, one place. The count's three conjuncts were inlined in scan_diff; the names disclosure needs the same three, so they moved into is_skipped_unknown_vocabulary_hunk. unread_vocabulary_names_in_diff runs only when the count is non-zero, and reuses parse_unified_diff/classify_assertion_change.

Two things stated in the code, same diff: the already-published ripgrep/tokio rows were taken with the narrower predicate and are not comparable to future readings (in the SKIPPED_UNKNOWN_VOCABULARY block and LIMITS item 6); and widening the predicate widens what can enter the counter, not what the matchers can see — the 19-hunk residue is still uncharacterised.

Measured, not assumed: render_blind_commits is fed from the same scan_diff count, so the widened predicate makes it reachable on a workspace layout with no second edit — demonstrated end-to-end on a scratch workspace repo (skipped line + names + blind-commit row), and --assert-macro check_that then moved the hunk into STRENGTHENED 1.

